<title>NIGERIA: Nigeria exceeds OPEC oil quota, agency says.</title>
<headline>Nigeria exceeds OPEC oil quota, agency says.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria overshot its OPEC quota of 1.865 million barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil production by 1,000 bpd in August, the News Agency of Nigeria said on Friday.</p>
<p>Quoting OPEC sources, the agency said Nigeria supplied its daily quota for the month, leaving the excess in strategic reserves.</p>
<p>According to a Reuter survey, Nigerian output in August was 2.05 million bpd, a significant recovery from the summer when production fell due to pipeline problems.</p>
<p>--Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317</p>
